1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:10,421
Chapter 6 The next day commenced as before, getting up and dressing by rush -light.

2
00:00:10,614 --> 00:00:14,579
But this morning we were obliged to dispense with the ceremony of washing.

3
00:00:15,379 --> 00:00:17,280
The water in the pictures was frozen.

4
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:22,159
A change had taken place in the weather the preceding evening and a keen northeast

5
00:00:22,161 --> 00:00:27,260
wind, whistling through the crevices of our bedroom windows all night long,

6
00:00:27,739 --> 00:00:32,680
had made us shiver in our beds, and turned the contents of the ures to ice.

7
00:00:33,159 --> 00:00:36,843
Before the long hour and a half of prayers and Bible

8
00:00:36,844 --> 00:00:39,920
reading was over, I felt ready to perish with cold.

9
00:00:41,049 --> 00:00:45,739
Breakfast time came at last, and this morning the porridge was not burnt.

10
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,860
The quality was eatable, the quantity small.

11
00:00:50,149 --> 00:00:52,139
How small my portion seemed.

12
00:00:52,879 --> 00:00:54,040
I wish it had been doubled.

13
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,692
In the course of the day I was enrolled a member of the fourth

14
00:00:58,693 --> 00:01:02,260
class, and regular tasks and occupations were assigned me.

15
00:01:03,219 --> 00:01:07,159
Hitherto, I had only been a spectator of the proceedings at Lowwood.

16
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:10,879
I was now to become an actor therein.

17
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:16,219
At first, being little accustomed to learn by heart.

18
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:19,739
The lessons appeared to me both long and difficult.

19
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:26,159
The frequent change from task to task two bewildered me, and I was glad when,

20
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:31,579
about three o'clock in the afternoon, miss Smith put into my hands a border of

21
00:01:31,581 --> 00:01:38,940
muslin two yards long, together with needle, thimble, etc., and sent me to sit

22
00:01:38,941 --> 00:01:43,659
in a quiet corner of the schoolroom, with directions to him the same.

23
00:01:45,159 --> 00:01:49,766
At that hour, most of the others were sowing likewise, but

24
00:01:49,768 --> 00:01:53,559
one class still stood round misscatchards chair reading.

25
00:01:54,600 --> 00:02:00,139
And as all was quiet, the subject of their lessons could be heard, together with the

26
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:04,879
manner in which each girl acquitted herself, and the animate versions or

27
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:07,700
commendations of misscatchard on the performance.

28
00:02:08,909 --> 00:02:10,379
It was English history.

29
00:02:11,459 --> 00:02:15,399
Among the readers, I observed my acquaintance of the veranda.

30
00:02:16,559 --> 00:02:20,959
At the commencement of the lesson, her place had been at the top of the

31
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:26,736
class, but for some error of pronunciation or some inattention

32
00:02:26,736 --> 00:02:31,079
to stops, she was suddenly sent to the very bottom.

33
00:02:32,469 --> 00:02:35,622
Even in that obscure position, misscatchard

34
00:02:35,623 --> 00:02:39,139
continued to make her an object of constant notice.

35
00:02:39,979 --> 00:02:43,700
She was continually addressing to her such phrases as the following.

36
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:48,159
Burns, such it seems was her name.

37
00:02:48,899 --> 00:02:52,440
The girls here were all called by their surnames as boys or elsewhere.

38
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:56,680
Burns, you are standing on the side of your shoe.

39
00:02:57,319 --> 00:02:59,020
Turn your toes out immediately.

40
00:03:00,239 --> 00:03:04,040
Burns, you poke your chin most unpleasantly, draw it in.

41
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:08,840
Burns, I insist on your holding your head up.

42
00:03:09,450 --> 00:03:13,860
I will not have you before me in that attitude, et cetera, et cetera.

43
00:03:14,729 --> 00:03:17,010
A chapter having been read through twice,

44
00:03:17,011 --> 00:03:20,281
the books were closed and the girls examined.

45
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:27,079
The lesson had comprised part of the reign of Charles I, and there were sundry

46
00:03:27,081 --> 00:03:29,566
questions about tonnage and poundage and ship

47
00:03:29,567 --> 00:03:33,059
money, which most of them appeared unable to answer.

48
00:03:34,129 --> 00:03:39,940
Still, every little difficulty was solved instantly when it reached Burns.

49
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:45,040
Her memory seemed to have retained the substance of the whole lesson,

50
00:03:45,879 --> 00:03:48,739
and she was ready with answers on every point.

51
00:03:50,204 --> 00:03:55,399
I kept expecting that misscatchard would praise her attention, but instead of that,

52
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,243
she suddenly cried out, you dirty, disagreeable

53
00:03:59,244 --> 00:04:02,319
girl, you have never cleaned your nails this morning.

54
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:06,479
Burns made no answer, I wondered at her silence.

55
00:04:07,889 --> 00:04:09,520
Why, thought I?

56
00:04:10,479 --> 00:04:14,399
Does she not explain that she could neither clean her nails nor wash her face

57
00:04:14,825 --> 00:04:16,059
as the water was frozen?

58
00:04:17,459 --> 00:04:24,040
My attention was now called off by Miss Smith, desiring me to hold a skein of thread.

59
00:04:24,510 --> 00:04:29,659
While she was winding it, she talked to me from time to time, asking whether I had

60
00:04:29,661 --> 00:04:34,100
ever been at school before, whether I could mark stitch, knit, et cetera.

61
00:04:35,409 --> 00:04:38,204
Till she dismissed me, I could not pursue

62
00:04:38,206 --> 00:04:41,640
my observations on misscatchard's movements.

63
00:04:42,610 --> 00:04:45,683
When I returned to my seat, that lady was just

64
00:04:45,683 --> 00:04:49,079
delivering an order of which I did not catch the import.

65
00:04:50,219 --> 00:04:55,780
But Burns immediately left the class, and going into the small inner room where

66
00:04:55,781 --> 00:05:00,084
the books were kept, returned in half a minute, carrying

67
00:05:00,084 --> 00:05:03,860
in her hand a bundle of twigs tied together at one end.

68
00:05:04,809 --> 00:05:09,659
This ominous tool she presented to misscatchard with a respectful curtsy,

69
00:05:10,409 --> 00:05:16,659
then she quietly and without being told, unloosed her pinnacle, and the teacher

70
00:05:16,661 --> 00:05:22,960
instantly and sharply inflicted on her neck a dozen strokes with the bunch of twigs.

71
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:29,200
Not a tear rose to Burns's eye, and while I paused from my sewing,

72
00:05:29,989 --> 00:05:32,364
because my fingers quivered at this spectacle

73
00:05:32,365 --> 00:05:35,420
with a sentiment of unavailing and impotent anger.

74
00:05:36,559 --> 00:05:40,340
Not a feature of her pensive face altered its ordinary expression.

75
00:05:41,940 --> 00:05:44,920
Hardened girl, exclaimed misscatchard.

76
00:05:45,639 --> 00:05:49,959
Nothing can correct you of your slatternly habits, carry the rod away.

77
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:52,420
Burns obeyed.

78
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:56,500
I looked at her narrowly as she emerged from the book closet.

79
00:05:57,565 --> 00:06:01,081
She was just putting back her handkerchief into her pocket,

80
00:06:01,181 --> 00:06:04,440
and the trace of a tear glistened on her thin cheek.

81
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:11,700
The play hour in the evening, I thought the pleasantest fraction of the day at lowwood.

82
00:06:12,319 --> 00:06:16,147
The bit of bread, the draft of coffee swallowed at five

83
00:06:16,148 --> 00:06:21,379
o'clock, had revived vitality if it had not satisfied hunger.

84
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:25,479
The long restraint of the day was slackened.

85
00:06:26,530 --> 00:06:29,200
The schoolroom felt warmer than in the morning.

86
00:06:30,149 --> 00:06:32,600
It's fires being allowed to burn a little more brightly.

87
00:06:33,270 --> 00:06:38,700
To supply, in some measure, the place of candles not yet introduced.

88
00:06:39,469 --> 00:06:44,457
The ruddy gloaming, the licensed uproar, the confusion

89
00:06:44,458 --> 00:06:47,879
of many voices gave one a welcome sense of liberty.

90
00:06:49,229 --> 00:06:53,299
On the evening of the day on which I had seen misscatchard flog her pupil,

91
00:06:53,559 --> 00:06:58,022
Burns, I wandered as usual among the forms and tables and

92
00:06:58,023 --> 00:07:03,159
laughing groups without a companion, yet not feeling lonely.

93
00:07:05,329 --> 00:07:10,059
When I passed the windows, I now and then lifted a blind and looked out,

94
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:11,540
it snowed fast.

95
00:07:12,610 --> 00:07:15,559
A drift was already forming against the lower pains.

96
00:07:16,579 --> 00:07:20,719
Putting my ear close to the window, I could distinguish from the gleeful

97
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:25,059
tumult within the disconsolate moan of the wind outside.

98
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:32,479
Probably, if I had lately left a good home and kind parents, this would have been the

99
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:36,059
hour when I should most keenly have regretted the separation.

100
00:07:37,379 --> 00:07:40,299
That wind would then have saddened my heart.

101
00:07:40,979 --> 00:07:47,260
This obscure chaos would have disturbed my peace, as it was, I derived from both a

102
00:07:47,261 --> 00:07:50,379
strange excitement and reckless and feverish.

103
00:07:51,110 --> 00:07:55,819
I wished the wind to howl more wildly, the gloom to deepen to darkness,

104
00:07:56,610 --> 00:07:58,760
and the confusion to rise to clamour.

105
00:07:59,950 --> 00:08:05,480
Jumping over forms and creeping under tables, I made my way to one of the fireplaces.

106
00:08:06,059 --> 00:08:12,540
There, kneeling by the high-wire fender, I found Burns, absorbed, silent,

107
00:08:13,180 --> 00:08:16,650
abstracted from all around her by the companionship of

108
00:08:16,652 --> 00:08:19,819
a book, which she read by the dim glare of the embers.

109
00:08:21,604 --> 00:08:24,180
Is it still resell us, I asked, coming behind her?

110
00:08:24,799 --> 00:08:27,840
Yes, she said, and I have just finished it.

111
00:08:28,579 --> 00:08:30,920
And in five minutes more, she shut it up.

112
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:32,700
I was glad of this.

113
00:08:33,899 --> 00:08:37,079
Now, thought I, I can perhaps get her to talk.

114
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:39,420
I sat down by her on the floor.

115
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:42,680
What is your name besides Burns?

116
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:45,100
Helen?

117
00:08:45,909 --> 00:08:47,229
Do you come a long way from here?

118
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:51,159
I come from a place farther north, quite on the borders of Scotland.

119
00:08:52,870 --> 00:08:54,200
Will you ever go back?

120
00:08:55,379 --> 00:08:58,799
I hope so, but nobody can be sure of the future.

121
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:02,159
You must wish to leave lowered?

122
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,799
No, why should I?

123
00:09:05,809 --> 00:09:09,336
I was sent to lowered to get an education, and it would

124
00:09:09,337 --> 00:09:12,340
be of no use going away until I have attained that object.

125
00:09:14,069 --> 00:09:17,260
But that teacher miscatchered is so cruel to you?

126
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:18,780
Cruel?

127
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:20,260
Not at all.

128
00:09:20,799 --> 00:09:21,799
She is severe.

129
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:23,940
She dislikes my faults.

130
00:09:25,184 --> 00:09:27,760
And if I were in your place, I should dislike her.

131
00:09:28,479 --> 00:09:29,579
I should resist her.

132
00:09:30,239 --> 00:09:34,059
If she struck me with that rod, I should get it from her hand.

133
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:36,079
I should break it under her nose.

134
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:40,180
Probably you would do nothing of the sort.

135
00:09:41,180 --> 00:09:45,879
But if you did, Mr. Brocklehurst would expel you from the school.

136
00:09:46,719 --> 00:09:48,879
That would be a great grief to your relations.

137
00:09:49,889 --> 00:09:54,159
It is far better to endure patiently a smart which nobody feels but yourself,

138
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:57,478
than to commit a hasty action whose evil

139
00:09:57,479 --> 00:10:01,320
consequences will extend to all connected with you.

140
00:10:01,629 --> 00:10:05,600
And besides, the Bible bids us return good for evil.

141
00:10:07,395 --> 00:10:12,079
But then it seems disgraceful to be flogged, and to be sent to stand in the

142
00:10:12,081 --> 00:10:16,120
middle of a room full of people, and you are such a great girl,

143
00:10:16,670 --> 00:10:19,819
I am far younger than you and I could not bear it.

144
00:10:21,430 --> 00:10:25,360
Yet it would be your duty to bear it, if you could not avoid it.

145
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,966
It is weak and silly to say you cannot bear

146
00:10:28,967 --> 00:10:32,661
what it is your fate to be required to bear.

147
00:10:34,149 --> 00:10:35,799
I heard her with wonder.

148
00:10:37,030 --> 00:10:41,319
I could not comprehend this doctrine of endurance, and still less could I

149
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:46,300
understand or sympathize with the forbearance she expressed for her chastiser.

150
00:10:47,389 --> 00:10:53,180
Still, I felt that Helen Burns considered things by a light invisible to my eyes.

151
00:10:54,200 --> 00:11:00,421
I suspected she might be right and I wrong, but I would not ponder the matter deeply.

152
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:03,360
Like Felix, I put it off to a more convenient season.

153
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:06,180
You say you have faults, Helen.

154
00:11:06,719 --> 00:11:07,719
What are they?

155
00:11:07,879 --> 00:11:09,479
To me, you seem very good.

156
00:11:10,665 --> 00:11:13,360
Then learn from me, not to judge by appearances.

157
00:11:14,239 --> 00:11:17,040
I am, as miscatured said, slatternly.

158
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:21,500
I seldom put and never keep things in order.

159
00:11:22,159 --> 00:11:23,159
I am careless.

160
00:11:23,639 --> 00:11:24,639
I forget rules.

161
00:11:25,299 --> 00:11:26,899
I read when I should learn my lessons.

162
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:31,468
I have no method, and sometimes I say, like you, I

163
00:11:31,469 --> 00:11:34,680
cannot bear to be subjected to systematic arrangements.

164
00:11:35,790 --> 00:11:38,391
This is all very provoking to miscatured, who

165
00:11:38,393 --> 00:11:41,380
is naturally neat, punctual and particular.

166
00:11:41,770 --> 00:11:43,819
And cross and cruel, I added.

167
00:11:44,559 --> 00:11:46,780
But Helen Burns would not admit my addition.

168
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,500
She kept silence.

169
00:11:49,979 --> 00:11:52,680
Is Ms. Temple as severe to you as miscatured?

170
00:11:54,079 --> 00:11:59,399
At the utterance of Ms. Temple's name, a soft smile flitted over her grave face.

171
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:03,059
Ms. Temple is full of goodness.

172
00:12:03,870 --> 00:12:07,479
It pains her to be severe to anyone, even the worst in the school.

173
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:10,719
She sees my errors and tells me of them gently.

174
00:12:11,629 --> 00:12:16,000
And if I do anything worthy of praise, she gives me my need liberally.

175
00:12:17,870 --> 00:12:22,979
One strong proof of my wretchedly defective nature is that even her

176
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:30,220
exposulations so mild, so rational, have not influenced to cure me of my faults.

177
00:12:30,469 --> 00:12:34,665
And even her praise, though I value it most highly,

178
00:12:34,666 --> 00:12:38,260
cannot stimulate me to continue to care and foresight.

179
00:12:39,940 --> 00:12:42,000
That is curious, said I.

180
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:44,739
It is so easy to be careful.

181
00:12:45,989 --> 00:12:48,639
For you, I have no doubt it is.

182
00:12:49,479 --> 00:12:53,739
I observed you in your class this morning, and saw you were closely attentive.

183
00:12:54,819 --> 00:12:57,472
Your thoughts never seemed to wander, while Ms.

184
00:12:57,474 --> 00:13:00,300
Miller explained the lesson and questioned you.

185
00:13:01,170 --> 00:13:05,979
Now mine continually rove away, when I should be listening to Ms.

186
00:13:06,159 --> 00:13:09,715
Scatchard, and collecting all she says with

187
00:13:09,716 --> 00:13:13,700
aciduity, often I lose the very sound of her voice.

188
00:13:14,530 --> 00:13:16,139
I fall into a sort of dream.

189
00:13:17,370 --> 00:13:22,620
Sometimes I think I am in Northumberland, and that the noises I hear around me are

190
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:28,060
the bubbling of a little brook, which runs through deep and near our house.

191
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:33,420
Then, when it comes to my turn to reply, I have to be awakened.

192
00:13:34,614 --> 00:13:38,920
And having heard nothing of what was read for listening to the visionary brook,

193
00:13:39,930 --> 00:13:44,719
I have no answer ready, yet how well you replied this afternoon.

194
00:13:46,309 --> 00:13:51,079
It was mere chance, the subject on which we had been reading had interested me.

195
00:13:52,389 --> 00:13:58,299
This afternoon, instead of dreaming of deep-den, I was wondering how a man who

196
00:13:58,300 --> 00:14:04,219
wished to do right could act so unjustly and unwisely as Charles I sometimes did.

197
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:11,440
And I thought what a pity it was that, with his integrity and conscientiousness,

198
00:14:12,389 --> 00:14:15,520
he could see no farther than the prerogatives of the crown.

199
00:14:16,639 --> 00:14:19,987
If he had but been able to look to a distance and see

200
00:14:19,988 --> 00:14:23,459
how what they call the spirit of the age was tending.

201
00:14:24,709 --> 00:14:30,360
Still, I like Charles, I respect him, I pity him poor murdered king.

202
00:14:31,239 --> 00:14:34,191
Yes, his enemies were the worst, they shed blood,

203
00:14:34,192 --> 00:14:37,819
they had no right to shed, how dare they kill him.

204
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,540
Helen was talking to herself now.

205
00:14:41,559 --> 00:14:45,730
She had forgotten I could not very well understand her that

206
00:14:45,731 --> 00:14:49,620
I was ignorant or nearly so of the subject she discussed.

207
00:14:50,579 --> 00:14:51,920
I recalled her to my level.

208
00:14:54,350 --> 00:14:57,940
And when Miss Temple teaches you, do your thoughts wander then?

209
00:14:59,329 --> 00:15:03,358
No, certainly not often, because Miss Temple has generally

210
00:15:03,359 --> 00:15:06,579
something to say which is newer than my own reflections.

211
00:15:08,059 --> 00:15:11,389
Her language is singularly agreeable to me, and the

212
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:15,379
information she communicates is often just what I wish to gain.

213
00:15:16,969 --> 00:15:19,100
Well then, with Miss Temple you are good?

214
00:15:20,399 --> 00:15:26,139
Yes, in a passive way, I make no effort, I follow as inclination guides me.

215
00:15:27,170 --> 00:15:29,239
There is no merit in such goodness.

216
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:34,399
A great deal, you are good to those who are good to you.

217
00:15:35,379 --> 00:15:37,200
It is all I ever desire to be.

218
00:15:38,559 --> 00:15:42,840
If people were always kind and obedient to those who are cruel and unjust,

219
00:15:44,059 --> 00:15:48,620
the wicked people would have it all their own way, they would never feel afraid,

220
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:53,399
and so they would never alter, but would grow worse and worse.

221
00:15:54,639 --> 00:15:59,899
When we are struck at without a reason, we should strike back again very hard,

222
00:16:00,579 --> 00:16:01,579
I'm sure we should.

223
00:16:02,409 --> 00:16:06,659
So hard as to teach the person, who struck us never to do it again.

224
00:16:08,549 --> 00:16:11,896
You will change your mind, I hope, when you grow

225
00:16:11,897 --> 00:16:15,139
older, as yet you are but a little untaught girl.

226
00:16:16,219 --> 00:16:22,399
But I feel this, Helen, I must dislike those who, whatever I do to please them,

227
00:16:23,079 --> 00:16:24,440
persist in disliking me.

228
00:16:25,235 --> 00:16:28,399
I must resist those who punish me unjustly.

229
00:16:29,235 --> 00:16:32,861
It is as natural as that I should love those who show me

230
00:16:32,861 --> 00:16:37,200
affection or submit to punishment when I feel it is deserved.

231
00:16:38,409 --> 00:16:40,827
Heathens and savage tribes hold that doctrine,

232
00:16:40,828 --> 00:16:44,020
but Christians and civilized nations disown it.

233
00:16:44,979 --> 00:16:45,979
How?

234
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:47,280
I don't understand.

235
00:16:48,299 --> 00:16:51,105
It is not violence that best overcomes hate,

236
00:16:51,106 --> 00:16:54,300
nor vengeance that most certainly heals injury.

237
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:55,860
What then?

238
00:16:56,610 --> 00:17:00,665
Read the New Testament and observe what Christ says and how

239
00:17:00,666 --> 00:17:04,920
he acts, make his word your rule and his conduct your example.

240
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:07,100
What does he say?

241
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:11,012
Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do

242
00:17:11,013 --> 00:17:14,600
good to them that hate you and despitefully use you.

243
00:17:15,690 --> 00:17:18,780
Then I should love Mrs. Reed, which I cannot do.

244
00:17:19,739 --> 00:17:22,559
I should bless her son, John, which is impossible.

245
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:30,600
In her turn, Helen Burns asked me to explain, and I proceeded forthwith to pour

246
00:17:30,601 --> 00:17:35,200
out in my own way the tale of my sufferings and resentments.

247
00:17:36,155 --> 00:17:41,740
Bitter and truckulent when excited, I spoke as I felt without reserve or softening.

248
00:17:42,299 --> 00:17:44,120
Helen heard me patiently to the end.

249
00:17:44,889 --> 00:17:48,020
I expected she would then make a remark, but she said nothing.

250
00:17:49,379 --> 00:17:52,299
Well, I asked impatiently.

251
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:56,139
Is not Mrs. Reed a hard-hearted, bad woman?

252
00:17:57,719 --> 00:18:02,105
She has been unkind to you, no doubt, because you see, she

253
00:18:02,106 --> 00:18:06,760
dislikes your cast of character as miscatcher does mine.

254
00:18:07,909 --> 00:18:13,659
But how minutely you remember all she has done and said to you, what a singularly

255
00:18:13,661 --> 00:18:17,739
deep impression her injustice seems to have made on your heart.

256
00:18:18,770 --> 00:18:21,639
No ill usage so brands its record on my feelings.

257
00:18:22,709 --> 00:18:25,518
Would you not be happier if you tried to forget her

258
00:18:25,519 --> 00:18:28,719
severity, together with the passionate emotions it excited?

259
00:18:30,549 --> 00:18:37,120
Life appears to me too short to be spent in nursing animosity or registering wrongs.

260
00:18:37,799 --> 00:18:43,540
We are, and must be, one and all, burdened with faults in this world.

261
00:18:44,309 --> 00:18:45,860
But the time will soon come.

262
00:18:46,579 --> 00:18:51,579
When, I trust, we shall put them off, in putting off our corruptible bodies,

263
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:56,940
when debasement and sin will fall from us with this comberous frame of flesh,

264
00:18:57,969 --> 00:19:00,299
and only the spark of the spirit will remain.

265
00:19:01,270 --> 00:19:05,322
The impalpable principle of light and thought, pure

266
00:19:05,323 --> 00:19:08,840
as when it left the creator to inspire the creature.

267
00:19:09,629 --> 00:19:11,959
Whence it came, it will return.

268
00:19:13,010 --> 00:19:18,479
Perhaps again to be communicated to some being higher than man, perhaps to pass

269
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:24,299
through gradations of glory from the pale human soul to brighten to the seraph.

270
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:30,479
Surely it will never on the contrary be suffered to degenerate from man to fiend?

271
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:33,260
No, I cannot believe that.

272
00:19:33,959 --> 00:19:38,399
I hold another creed, which no one ever taught me, and which I seldom mention,

273
00:19:39,270 --> 00:19:44,559
but in which I delight, and to which I cling, for it extends hope to all.

274
00:19:45,469 --> 00:19:51,059
It makes eternity a rest, a mighty home, not a terror and an abyss.

275
00:19:51,879 --> 00:19:54,406
Besides, with this creed, I can so clearly

276
00:19:54,407 --> 00:19:58,300
distinguish between the criminal and his crime.

277
00:19:58,590 --> 00:20:02,319
I can so sincerely forgive the first while I appore the last.

278
00:20:02,899 --> 00:20:05,760
With this creed, revenge never worries my heart.

279
00:20:06,540 --> 00:20:09,000
Degradation and never too deeply disgusts me.

280
00:20:09,799 --> 00:20:11,479
Injustice never crushes me too low.

281
00:20:12,350 --> 00:20:14,559
I live in calm, looking to the end.

282
00:20:16,239 --> 00:20:22,001
Helen's head, always drooping, sank a little lower as she finished this sentence.

283
00:20:22,329 --> 00:20:25,852
I saw by her look she wished no longer to talk to

284
00:20:25,852 --> 00:20:28,980
me, but rather to converse with her own thoughts.

285
00:20:29,930 --> 00:20:32,520
She was not allowed much time for meditation.

286
00:20:33,590 --> 00:20:39,520
A monitor, a great, rough girl, presently came up, exclaiming in a strong,

287
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:40,760
cumble and accent.

288
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:47,879
Helen burns, if you don't go and put your drawer in order and fold up your work this

289
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:51,040
minute, I'll tell Ms. Scratchard to come and look at it.

290
00:20:52,670 --> 00:20:57,039
Helen's side, as her reverie fled and getting up,

291
00:20:57,040 --> 00:21:01,280
obeyed the monitor without reply as without delay.
